    "user_request_original": "Design a multi-cavity bandpass filter on fused silica substrate. Stack topology: air incident medium, then 6 repeated pairs of SiO2 (Gao) and al2o3 (SiO2 (Gao) first), followed by a SiO2 (Gao) defect cavity, then 4 repeated pairs of al2o3 and SiO2 (Gao) (al2o3 first), followed by an al2o3 defect cavity, then 4 repeated pairs of SiO2 (Gao) and al2o3 (SiO2 (Gao) first), followed by a SiO2 (Gao) defect cavity, then 6 repeated pairs of al2o3 and SiO2 (Gao) (al2o3 first), terminating on SiO2 (Gao) substrate. Total film layers: 25. All 25 layer thicknesses are optimizable design variables. Wavelength bands: maximize transmittance in 255-280 nm, minimize transmittance in 300-700 nm and 700-1100 nm. No metal layers. Normal incidence, unpolarized light. Total layers must not exceed 30.",
